#%PAM-1.0
# PAM stack for sudo-rs in the c2s rescue image.
#
# sudo-rs calls pam_start()/pam_authenticate()/pam_acct_mgmt()/pam_open_session()
# unconditionally and aborts if the stack is missing ("sudo: PAM error:
# Critical error - immediate abort").  The rescue image grants rights with
# NOPASSWD rules, so no authentication module is needed: pam_permit always
# succeeds.  All four stacks (auth / account / password / session) must be
# present, otherwise sudo-rs fails with a PAM error.
auth     required pam_permit.so
account  required pam_permit.so
password required pam_permit.so
session  required pam_permit.so
